nce = Ticker/SchedulerBinding frames driven by the engine vsync; the Linux GTK embedder registers no vsync callback, so the engine uses its fallback vsync waiter with a fixed 1/60 s tick (engine source shell/common/vsync_waiter_fallback.cc). No public/documented API uncaps it, so uncapped -> pacing \"60-only\". gc = null: Dart exposes no GC counters in AOT release. Warm-up 2 s; script time frozen at 0 during warm-up. images: Image(ResizeImage(FileImage, width 128, height 128)) per cell (decode at 128x128 by the engine off the UI isolate, kept in ImageCache). decode_total_ms = sum over images of wall time from first build of the cell to its first frame (file read + decode + scheduling, incl. CPU contention with llvmpipe); counters cover the whole run incl. warm-up. GridView.builder 10 columns x 128 px; scroll = triangle wave over the grid at 3000 px/s; zoom 1->3->1 over 6 s (Transform) with a sinusoidal pan; during warm-up the script is frozen at t=0.","unsupported":null}